    "problemStatement": "You are given an undirected tree of NNN nodes. A positive weight WiW_iWi​ is assigned to the node iii for all 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.\n\nFor all 1≤j≤N−11 \\le j \\le N-11≤j≤N−1, the jjj-th edge connects the nodes uju_juj​ and vjv_jvj​, and has a restriction value of RjR_jRj​.\n\nAn array A1,A2,⋯ ,ANA_1, A_2, \\cdots, A_NA1​,A2​,⋯,AN​ consisting of NNN non-negative integers is called **valid** if:\n\n\nFor all 1≤j≤N−11 \\le j \\leq N-11≤j≤N−1, the condition Auj+Avj≤RjA_{u_j}+A_{v_j} \\le R_jAuj​​+Avj​​≤Rj​ holds.\nThe **profit** of a **valid** array AAA is defined as profit(A)=∑i=1NAi⋅Wiprofit(A)=\\sum_{i=1}^N A_i \\cdot W_iprofit(A)=∑i=1N​Ai​⋅Wi​\n\nFind the maximum possible value of profit(A)profit(A)profit(A) for some valid array AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the number of nodes in the tree.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers W1,W2,⋯ ,WNW_1, W_2, \\cdots, W_NW1​,W2​,⋯,WN​ denoting the weights assigned to every node.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines contain three space-separated integers each, with the jjj-th line containing uju_juj​, vjv_jvj​, and RjR_jRj​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum possible value of profit(A)profit(A)profit(A).",
